# Reuse existing renderers

Before adding any new field, form, or table UI for taxonomy/model data:

1. **Look first** — is there already a shared renderer?
   - Object Form / Table / Compact → `WTTObjectRender` (`assets/js/wtt-object-render.js`): `renderForm`, `renderTable`, `renderCompact`, `mount`
   - Field cells / Registry → same module + `WTTMediaRender` / node-render
   - Admin preview → tree-admin calls into those shared surfaces (P0–P4 rules)
2. **Reuse** that API (same chrome for admin preview, Object View, Table view).
3. If nothing fits and you would invent a **new renderer** or **hard-coded** `<input>`/`<table>` for the same job → **stop and ask the user** before implementing.

## Settings cascade → paint (locked)

Defaults cascade detail→model (Präfix → BU → Unit type → Model). Paint **must** follow Preferred, Q117 Presentation, Hide, Mult, Bindung, walk/Relation overrides.

- **Host Preview** = host Preferred only.
- **Nested attribute cell** = attribute type Preferred (`paintStructureEmbed` / `resolveFieldPreferredPaint`) — not invent Form when Compact is set.
- **No hardcoding** by display name, path, or special-case node. Hardcode **only** inside a renderer for that renderer’s own chrome, **current layer only**.

See [preview-checkpoints.mdc](preview-checkpoints.mdc) and [project-plan Presentation surfaces](../../docs/plans/project-plan.md#presentation-surfaces-architecture).

## Taxo blocks

| Block | Must use |
|-------|----------|
| `taxo/object-view` | `WTTObjectRender.mount` / Form·Table·Compact |
| `taxo/collection-table` (Taxo Table view) | `WTTObjectRender.renderTable` for model dataset rows (columns = attributes) |

Do not hand-build attribute cells in block `edit.js` when `renderTable` / `paintFieldContent` already cover the type.

## Do / don’t

- **Do** extend the shared renderer when a type or layout is missing.
- **Do** ask when unsure whether an existing surface applies.
- **Do** honour nested type Preferred / Presentation / Hide when embedding structure fields.
- **Don’t** add a parallel table/form “just for the block”.
- **Don’t** show raw type labels in headers as a substitute for proper field views (`Name (text)` + bare `<input>`).
- **Don’t** special-case paint by node display name or invent host chrome that ignores walk settings.

Related: [choosers.mdc](choosers.mdc) (one chooser per purpose), [preview-checkpoints.mdc](preview-checkpoints.mdc) (unified preview).
